% lps-converted-from: hunger.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program hunger.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the events are:
    *a thing* becomes hungry.
    *a thing* wanders near *a second thing*.

the actions are:
    *a thing* picks up *a second thing*; known as pick_up.
    *a thing* eats *a second thing*; known as eat.

the fluents are:
    the hungry is *a thing*; known as hungry.
    *a thing* is near *a second thing*; known as near.
    *a thing* has *a second thing*.

the templates are:
    the food is *a thing*; known as food.

the knowledge base hunger includes:

initially me is near apple.

when a thing becomes hungry
then the hungry is the thing.

when a thing wanders near a second thing
then the thing is near the second thing.

when a thing picks up a second thing
then the thing has the second thing.

when a thing eats a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing has the second thing.

when a thing eats a second thing
then it is not the case that the hungry is the thing.

the food is apple.

the food is bread.

if the hungry is a thing at a time
then the thing has a second thing at a second time
    and the food is the second thing
    and the thing eats the second thing from the second time.

if the hungry is a thing
    and the thing is near a second thing
    and the food is the second thing
    and it is not the case that the thing has the second thing
then the thing picks up the second thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing picks up a second thing
    and it is not the case that the thing is near the second thing.


scenario one is:
    me becomes hungry from 2 to 3.
